; regression test: `def`'s right-hand-side scan (`extract_by_condition`, which has no
; bound-variable awareness at all -- it only ever "works" in practice because idiomatic
; Kurt uses `$`-prefixed schema variables in bound positions here, which are
; unconditionally classified as variables regardless) must recognize `forall`/`exists`
; themselves as already-classified vocabulary, not as unclassified "new symbols" the RHS
; isn't allowed to contain. See doc/kurt-soundness.md §2.1's closing note: this broke
; when `forall`/`exists` were first hard-coded via the same pattern as `sub` (`.used`
; without `const`) -- fixed by registering them `const` instead, matching
; `true`/`implies`/`and`. Found via proofs/linear-algebra/injective2.kurt, which
; exercises the same thing in a full proof (there with `$x`/`$y`, as here).
load logic
bool Q
arity Q 1
const z
use Q z
def p iff forall $x Q $x
true
;;; Proof checked.
